iods for Class II and Class III services for non-\npediatric members.\nReplace the first paragraph of the\nWhen Your Benefits Begin subsection with the following:\nNOTE: THE LANGUAGE IN BOLD IS NEW TO YOUR CERTIFICATE.\nWhen Your Benefits Begin\nMost benefits are available on the effective date of your contract. However,\na waiting period applies to Class II and Class III services as follows:\n\u2022 A 6-month waiting period applies to Class II services except for\ndental sealants and emergency palliative treatments.\n\u2022 A 12-month waiting period applies to Class III services.\nThese waiting periods apply only to non-pediatric members.\nBenefits become effective on the day after the last day of the\nwaiting period.\nFor a 12-month waiting period, if your contract becomes\neffective on July 1, the last date of the waiting period will be\nJune 30 of the following year. Benefits become available on\nJuly 1 of that year.\nClass I benefits are not affected by this rider.\n2 \u00a9 2025 Blue Cross Blue Shield of Michigan", "lemma_text": "this rider change the coverage in your certificate your rider and certificate be mean to be read together it be important to review this change to understand how your coverage have change section 1 information about your contract what s change this rider add wait period for class ii and class iii service for non pediatric member replace the first paragraph of the when your benefit begin subsection with the following note the language in bold be new to your certificate when your benefit begin most benefit be available on the effective date of your contract however a wait period apply to class ii and class iii service as follow a 6 month wait period apply to class ii service except for dental sealant and emergency palliative treatment a 12 month wait period apply to class iii service this wait period apply only to non pediatric member benefit become effective on the day after the last day of the wait period for a 12 month wait period if